  "assumption_notes": {
    "event_count": "2 active device equivalents * 8h * 3600 / 30s * 2 sources = 3840. Synthetic reference, not measured typical usage.",
    "payload": "350B initial logical payload premise; wire includes envelope. No implication 350B PostgreSQL physical row. Payload350B remains a logical mass field, not an independent costdriver; change wire/hot/archive fields together for a larger-event scenario.",
    "wire": "500B/event rounded reference; synthetic sample486.665B nested JSON and518.665B escaped JSON envelope, not encrypted; wire500 is not a PostgreSQL physical row size.",
    "hot": "700 B/event cost reference retained with margin. Separate local 1M synthetic PostgreSQL 18.6 benchmark measured 563.716096 B/event including table + 4 indexes (431.77 MB table, 131.95 MB indexes), excluding replica, backup and bloat. SQLite 10M measured 482.7 B/event does not establish PG size. Neither local test establishes cloud DB capacity.",
    "archive": "100B/event reference; separate10M synthetic ParquetZSTD result52.03B/event. Sensitive tocardinality,stringsandencryption;compressbeforeclientencryption.",
    "backup": "Retained billed backup data=2xhot footprint as a storage budget, not two independent DR locations nor a promised seven-day PITR policy.",
    "cpu": "10ms CPU/request,100mswall,4 overlappingrequests are UNMEASURED inputs. Amortizedinstancebilltime=max(wall/overlap,CPU/targetutilization); one-userisolated requestsroundwallto100ms. CPU sensitivity1/10/100ms,wall100/1000ms. This is not a runtimebenchmark nor a capacityforecast.",
    "archive_age": "Monthly run-rate after five years of history for a constant user population; NOT cumulative five-year bill and not first-month bill.",
    "blind": "Blind-sync PG contains assumed1MB/user controlmetadata; encrypted recent batches are temporaryobjects1day then compacted client-side daily. Same API and logical raw-sync egress held for conservative comparison; clientcompactionwork notpriced. Alternative blind_sync_pg_staging uses1day of opaque encrypted PG staging plus controlmetadata, withsame hotbytes/event assumption; onlydaily objects reachobjectstore. Server cannot query plaintext in either variant.",
    "cloudflare_postgres": "Scaleway external PostgreSQL deliberately held equal to Scaleway standalone comparison to isolate compute/storage differences. Not a claim it is the best external PG supplier.",
    "byte_units": "GCP/AWS storage priced in GiB=2^30 bytes. Scaleway/R2 storage modeled advertised GB=10^9 (interpretation uncertainty up to7.4%; confirm invoices). Hetzner TB decimal. Scaleway Containers RAM conversion follows official FAQ128MB=0.125GB, thus modeled1:1 to configuredGiB.",
    "HA": "Cloud SQL/RDS commercialprofiles automatic cross-AZ; Scaleway and externalPGprofile sameDC/rackHA only. Hetzner2VMreference is NOT an HA implementation.",
    "hetzner": "Only currentVM+IPv4+20%rootdiskbackup+object storage+logicalPGbackup priced; data volumes/LB/quorum unpriced. Not directly comparabletotal.",
    "downloads": "Default2 additional APIrequests per ingestbatch for2 receivingdevices; ratio0 sensitivity means piggyback/directpresignedobjectreads. Wireegresscopies remain2. Retries andmanifestpolling are additional.",
    "realtime": "Bulk-sync baseline is NOT realtime. 5s batch sensitivity sends scheduled requests even if empty; latency still adds network/processing. Persistent connection floor uses2devices/user*8h/day,1vCPU/0.5GiB instances: Cloud Run instance-based 100/250/1000 connections (latter configuration ceiling, NOT capacity guarantee), Scaleway80 configuration ceiling and200 maxscale. Shared bulk API/free pool once; excludes reconnect/fanout/pubsub, scale-down tails and spare concurrency slots."
  },
